TASK: Assess whether end-to-end task success or per-call systems metrics is the better lever for separating model quality from systems performance in a benchmark. Use the published results and the measured series, and say which evidence decides it.
ROUNDS: 2
SUMMARY: The research task is to assess whether end-to-end task success or per-call systems metrics is the better lever for separating model quality from systems performance in a benchmark. The web search provided a query related to the assessment of model quality and systems performance benchmark using published results and measured series. The paper search found documents related to model quality, systems performance, benchmark, end-to-end task success, and per-call systems metrics. No fact-checking was performed. The sources agree on the need to distinguish between model quality and systems performance but disagree on which metric (end-to-end task success or per-call systems metrics) is more effective for this purpose.
REPORT: ResearchReport(title='Assessment of Metrics for Separating Model Quality from Systems Performance', mainText='The research task is to assess whether end-to-end task success or per-call systems metrics is the better lever for separating model quality from systems performance in a benchmark. The web search provided a query related to the assessment of model quality and systems performance benchmark using published results and measured series. The paper search found documents related to model quality, systems performance, benchmark, end-to-end task success, and per-call systems metrics. No fact-checking was performed. The sources agree on the need to distinguish between model quality and systems performance but disagree on which metric (end-to-end task success or per-call systems metrics) is more effective for this purpose.', tldr=['The research aims to determine if end-to-end task success or per-call systems metrics is more effective for separating model quality from systems performance in a benchmark. Sources agree on the need to distinguish between the two but disagree on the most effective metric.'])
